; TREE.LGO - a recursive tree: every branch carries two smaller trees
;
; This is the classic example of recursion in Logo. TREE draws a trunk,
; then calls TREE twice for the two branches, each a bit shorter.
; When the branches get small enough it stops.
;
; Debugger tip: put a breakpoint on the "forward :size" line (click in
; the margin) and press F5. Then open the Call Stack tab and press F11
; a few times: you can see one TREE waiting inside another.

to tree :size
  if :size < 6 [stop]
  setpensize :size / 8
  setpencolor ifelse :size < 15 [[60 160 70]] [[110 70 40]]
  forward :size
  left 25
  tree :size * 0.72
  right 50
  tree :size * 0.72
  left 25
  back :size
end

clearscreen
penup setxy 0 -250 pendown
tree 110
hideturtle
